      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to first analyze the pattern of the sequence and then compute the sum of the terms.\n\nThe sequence given is:\n\\[1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\]\n\nWe observe that the sequence alternates between positive and negative terms. Let's identify the pattern of the terms:\n- The first term is \\(1\\).\n- The second term is \\(-4\\).\n- The third term is \\(7\\).\n- The fourth term is \\(-10\\).\n- And so on.\n\nWe can separate the sequence into groups of four terms:\n\\[\n(1 - 4 + 7 - 10) + (13 - 16 + 19 - 22) + \\cdots + (49 - 52 + 55)\n\\]\n\nEach group of four terms can be simplified:\n\\[\na + b - c - d\n\\]\nWhere \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = -4\\), \\(c = 7\\), and \\(d = -10\\).\n\nLet's compute the sum of one group:\n\\[\n1 - 4 + 7 - 10 = (1 + 7) - (4 + 10) = 8 - 14 = -6\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, for the next group:\n\\[\n13 - 16 + 19 - 22 = (13 + 19) - (16 + 22) = 32 - 38 = -6\n\\]\n\nWe observe that each group of four terms sums to \\(-6\\).\n\nNext, we need to determine the number of such groups in the sequence. The sequence ends with \\(55\\), and we can count the number of four-term groups:\n- The first group is \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10\\).\n- The second group is \\(13 - 16 + 19 - 22\\).\n- The third group is \\(23 - 26 + 29 - 32\\).\n- And so on...\n\nThe last group before \\(55\\) is:\n\\[49 - 52 + 55\\]\n\nWe need to check how many groups there are:\n1. First group: \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 = -6\\)\n2. Second group: \\(13 - 16 + 19 - 22 = -6\\)\n3. Third group: \\(23 - 26 + 29 - 32 = -6\\)\n4. Fourth group: \\(35 - 38 + 41 - 44 = -6\\)\n5. Fifth group: \\(43 - 46 + 49 - 52 = -6\\)\n\nThus, we have \\(5\\) complete groups of four terms each, and the last term \\(49 - 52 + 55 = 12\\).\n\nTherefore, the total sum of the sequence is:\n\\[\n5 \\times (-6) + 12\n\\]\n\nCalculating this:\n\\[\n5 \\times (-6) = -30\n\\]\n\\[\n-30 + 12 = -18\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the given expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-18}\n\\]",
