      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), we need to identify the pattern and simplify the series step by step.\n\nFirst, let's observe the pattern in the series. The series alternates between adding and subtracting terms. The terms are:\n\\[1, -4, 7, -10, 13, -16, \\ldots, 49, -52, 55\\]\n\nWe can group the terms in pairs:\n\\[(1 - 4) + (7 - 10) + (13 - 16) + \\cdots + (49 - 52) + 55\\]\n\nEach pair can be simplified as:\n\\[1 - 4 = -3\\]\n\\[7 - 10 = -3\\]\n\\[13 - 16 = -3\\]\n\\[\\vdots\\]\n\\[49 - 52 = -3\\]\n\nSo, each pair of terms alternates between positive and negative 3. There are 14 pairs in total (from \\(1\\) to \\(55\\), there are 14 terms, and the last term \\(55\\) is positive).\n\nThe sum of each pair is \\(-3\\), so the sum of all 14 pairs is:\n\\[-3 \\times 14 = -42\\]\n\nNow, we need to add the last term, which is \\(55\\):\n\\[-42 + 55 = 13\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is:\n\\[\\boxed{13}\\]",
